   The user asked me to build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the React application already scaffolded in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope). The stack is described in spec/stack.md. Work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/ (01 through 07) which must be implemented in order. spec/README.md is stated to be the complete specification: I must not ask any questions, and where it is silent I should choose the simplest option that satisfies it. The task finishes only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. No other user messages were given — this is the single, complete initial instruction, and all work since has been autonomous implementation based on reading the spec and tickets.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Nx 23 monorepo with React 19 + Vite + React Router 6 (BrowserRouter) + SCSS + Vitest + ESLint
   - MUI 9 (@mui/material 9.4.0, @mui/icons-material) and MUI X Date Pickers 9.14.0 with dayjs 1.11.23 adapter
   - json-server 0.17.4 backend serving db.json at http://localhost:3000 (GET /movies, /movies/:id, /screenings, /screenings?date=, /screenings?movieId=, /screenings/:id, POST /reservations)
   - sessionStorage-persisted "booking in progress" state machine with strict route-guard semantics (route 2 requires screening exists; routes 3/4 require unpaid booking matching screening id with ≥1 seat; route 5 requires paid booking) — guards run once per route entry, not on every state change
   - Auditorium geometry: 15 rows × 24 columns, two aisles (between cols 4/5 and 20/21), entrance gap (rows 1-10 missing cols 1-4, not an aisle), accessible seats (row 1, cols 10-15), couches (row 15, 12 couches of 2 columns each) — total 308 selectable elements
   - Exact data-testid contract (section 9 of spec) — names/attributes must match exactly, not be renamed/abbreviated, and must only exist conditionally per spec (e.g., `movies-loading` only while loading, `-error` elements only while shown)
   - Seat pricing by row band (25/32/39 PLN) and couch flat price (89 PLN)
   - Toast system: single toast at a time, 4-second display, replaced instantly by new toasts
   - Checkout validation rules: required/min-length/email regex/match/phone regex/terms-required, with "touched" (blur-based) display logic that is NOT persisted (resets on fresh mount) while the typed values ARE persisted in the booking
   - TypeScript strict mode type-checking via `tsc -b --noEmit` (separate from `vite build`, which does not type-check since it uses esbuild)
   - MUI slotProps API quirks: TextField's `inputLabel`/`htmlInput` slots and Checkbox's `input` slot don't type-accept arbitrary `data-testid` keys directly; casting the literal `as object` satisfies structural typing (since the target SlotProps types have all-optional properties) without resorting to `any`
   - ESLint rule `@typescript-eslint/no-non-null-assertion` flags `!` non-null assertions as warnings in this codebase

