   - Solved the column-alignment geometry problem (AC-08: "column 12 at the same horizontal position in every row") by deriving couch/aisle/placeholder pixel widths mathematically from a single `SEAT_SIZE`/`GAP` pair so that couch-based rows (row 15) and entrance-gap rows (1-10) occupy exactly the same total block widths as fully-seated rows (11-14), guaranteeing pixel alignment via identical structural templates rather than hardcoded independent widths.
