5. Problem Solving:
   - Solved the column-alignment geometry problem (AC-08: "column 12 at the same horizontal position in every row") by deriving couch/aisle/placeholder pixel widths mathematically from a single `SEAT_SIZE`/`GAP` pair so that couch-based rows (row 15) and entrance-gap rows (1-10) occupy exactly the same total block widths as fully-seated rows (11-14), guaranteeing pixel alignment via identical structural templates rather than hardcoded independent widths.
   - Solved the booking-item ordering/grouping problem (summary ordered by row then column, selected-seats-panel grouped by row, couch pairs reconstructed from flat seat-id arrays) via one shared `buildBookingItems`/`summarizeByRow` pair of functions in `lib/seats.ts`, reused across `SelectedSeatsPanel`, `Summary`, and the reservation POST payload (`items.flatMap(item => item.ids)` for "seats in summary order, couch as its two identifiers").
   - Solved the route-guard-vs-in-screen-navigation conflict (spec: guards check "when a route is entered... not while the customer stays on a screen") via `useRef`-based one-time-per-mount guard hooks, rather than naive `useEffect` with full dependency arrays that would re-fire on every booking mutation (which would have incorrectly redirected the Summary screen to `/` when `Remove` empties the seat list, instead of letting the explicit `navigate(/seats)` call in `handleRemove` take effect).
   - Solved MUI typing friction for data-testid placement on internal library sub-elements (labels, native inputs) via targeted `as object` casts rather than blanket `any`, preserving most type safety while satisfying the spec's exact `data-testid` contract (section 9.7: "identifiers of the five text fields, the terms checkbox and the datepicker may be placed either on the native `<input>` itself or on the UI library's component element that contains it").
   - **Ongoing/unresolved**: the 5 ESLint non-null-assertion warnings in SeatMap.tsx (lint target technically "succeeds" with warnings only, so it doesn't block `pnpm nx build cinescope`, but should still be cleaned up per the coding-quality guidelines in my instructions, and to keep the codebase idiomatic).

